# Percentage scaling promotes integers to decimal

Verifies an integer amount scaled by a decimal rate promotes to decimal. Multiplying 200 by 50% in both operand orders yields the decimal 100.00 instead of truncating to an integer result.

>>> source
count: int = 200
half: decimal = 50%
print(count * half)
print(half * count)

<<< stdout
100.00
100.00

<<< stderr
